user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-10-19T05:28:37Z","updated_at":"2023-10-19T05:31:48Z","body":"Ok this is weird but I tried the check_license tool on the first 1/2 and did NOT get any matching SPDX licenses although @whot is correct that it seems to be a perfect match.  \r\n\r\nFirst 1/2 of this also matches another Scancode key - [font-alias](https://scancode-licensedb.aboutcode.org/font-alias.html) but it doesn't include \"Permission is granted to anyone to use, distribute and modify this file in any way, provided that the above copyright notice is left intact and the author of the modification summarizes the changes in this header. This file is distributed without any expressed or implied warranty.\"\r\n\r\nSince this is the second one that I have seen like this - what is our approach vis-a-vis other org's license IDs???","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1770040926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1781203091","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2173#issuecomment-1781203091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2173","id":1781203091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85qKwCT","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-10-26T14:06:32Z","updated_at":"2023-10-26T14:06:32Z","body":"@Pizza-Ria I suspect that the check-license tool might not be seeing it because [Cronyx](https://spdx.org/licenses/Cronyx.html) (the matching license) was just added in the 3.22 release. So the check-license tool might not be updated yet (I haven't checked), and/or the version of the extension you're using might not have it yet.\r\n\r\nI ran into a similar issue using Google to try to search for this text -- I'm guessing the Google caches haven't yet crawled the license texts at https://spdx.org/licenses since the latest release.\r\n\r\nRegarding license IDs used by Scancode or other third parties, I think they can perhaps be informative but should not be determinative. If an identifier used by a third party fits with typical SPDX formatting and choices, then I'm fine with using it, but I think we should feel free to use the names / IDs that we think are most appropriate. Here, if only part of the license text matches a Scancode license, then I don't think we need to focus much on the naming they've used for the different one.\r\n\r\nHere, I'm +1 to add this as a simple, permissive and historical license used in Fedora.\r\n\r\nFor name / ID, I might go with \"xkeyboard-config-Zinoviev\" as ID and \"xkeyboard-config Zinoviev License\" as the name? I don't have a strong feeling on this, but I think that the Cronyx licenses is non-distinctive enough -- and the added requirement in the second paragraph is different enough -- that including \"Cronyx-\" in the license ID may not be helpful here.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1781203091/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1782087581","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2173#issuecomment-1782087581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2173","id":1782087581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85qOH-d","user":{"login":"whot","id":1487352,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODczNTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487352?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whot","html_url":"https://github.com/whot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whot/starred{/own